  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">We Effect-Reincorporation Colombia 2018-2022 - We Effect-Reincorporation Colombia-2018-2022</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">We Effect-Reincorporation Colombia 2018-2022</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the intervention is to contribute to peacebuilding in Colombia through the reintegration of FARC ex-combatants and their full exercise of citizenship and related rights in conditions of equality.

The intervention will contribute specifically to the establishment and development of ECOMUN, the cooperative organisation of ex-FARC combatants, as a vehicle for transformation and for the creation of conditions and mechanisms for effective reincorporation of ex-combatant men and women within the framework of a social, solidarity and environmentally sustainable economy.

Expected results by the end of the intervention are:

Result 1: ECOMUN is strengthened as a democratic cooperative organisation under the principles of the solidarity economy for the effective participation of ex-combatant women and men and the communities surrounding the reincorporation areas, within the framework of the peace agreements implementation.

Result 2: ECOMUNs grassroots, ex-combatant women and men and the communities surrounding the reincorporation areas have identified concrete initiatives for community reincorporation and collaboration in social and economic life at the local level.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Detta &#xe4;r ett projektst&#xf6;d f&#xf6;r organisations- och kapacitetsutveckling av ECOMUN och lokala kooperativ f&#xf6;r demobiliserade FARC-medlemmar, genom den svenska civilsamh&#xe4;llesorganisationen We Effect.

Insatsen &#xe4;mnar att bidra till genomf&#xf6;randet av fredsavtalet mellan Colombias regering och FARC och d&#xe4;rmed till en varaktig fred med m&#xe4;nsklig s&#xe4;kerhet, genom att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra f&#xf6;ruts&#xe4;ttningarna f&#xf6;r den socioekonomiska &#xe5;terintegreringen av f&#xf6;re detta gerillasoldater i samh&#xe4;llet, med fokus p&#xe5; socialt och milj&#xf6;m&#xe4;ssigt h&#xe5;llbar produktiv syssels&#xe4;ttning och j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhetsintegrering.
ECOMUN &#xe4;r den organisation som FARC f&#xf6;reslagit i syfte att st&#xf6;dja och st&#xe4;rka de lokala kooperativ som bildats av f&#xf6;re detta soldater. Projektet har utvecklats tillsammans med ECOMUN och We Effect tillhandah&#xe5;ller resurser och specialiserad r&#xe5;dgivning f&#xf6;r bildandet av organisationen, liksom dess m&#xf6;jligheter att verka och utvecklas till en ledande organisation f&#xf6;r den kollektiva &#xe5;terintegreringsprocessen, i linje med de f&#xf6;re detta soldaternas egna behov och &#xf6;nskem&#xe5;l. Ingen vidaref&#xf6;rmedling av medel sker till ECOMUN eller de lokala kooperativen.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is a project support for organizational and capacity development of ECOMUN and local cooperatives for demobilized FARC members, through the Swedish civil society organization We Effect.

The effort aims to contribute to the implementation of the peace agreement between the Government of Colombia and the FARC and thus to a lasting peace with human security, by improving the conditions for the socio-economic reincorporation of former guerrilla soldiers into society, focusing on socially and environmentally sustainable productive activities and gender integration.
ECOMUN is the organization proposed by the FARC in order to support and strengthen the local cooperatives formed by their ex-combatants. The project has been developed together with ECOMUN and We Effect provides resources and specialized advice for the formalization of the organization, as well as its possibilities to operate and develop into a leading organization for the collective reintegration process, in line with the ex-combatants&apos; own needs and wishes. No transfer of funds takes place to ECOMUN or the local cooperatives.</narrative>
  </description>
